**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Promote to library writes the promoted value as the entry's next version in the library database and snapshots that version into the kit (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database'; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'; 001 §E 'a snapshot of every library version it uses'; the S11.5 brief 'It is then snapshotted into the kit (S4.2)'). It REUSES the import seam's write (`CatalogueImportProxy.putEntryVersion` and `CatalogueImportContext.sealEntry`, step 94), the one path that stores a whole entry version with its own provenance and hash, and the kit's snapshot (`KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences`, step 139, which pins the version before it writes `library/<GUID>@v<n><kind extension>`), so no library or kit verb is added. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. In `StudyPublishing.fs`, after `promotionSubjectsWith` (step 407): (1) `PublishError` gains `PromotionImportErr of error : CatalogueImportError` (`the library refused the promoted version: <the error's describe>`), `PromotionEntryErr of error : LibraryEntryError` (`the promoted entry could not be built: <the error's describe>`) and `PromotionKitErr of error : KitLibraryError` (`the kit could not snapshot the promoted version: <the error's describe>`). (2) On a `type KitLibraryContext with` extension (step 139): `member this.promoteMaterial (study : Study) (run : FitRun) (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<LibraryVersionRef, PublishError>` and `member this.promoteBlackBox (run : FitRun) (item : Item) (choice : ItemModelChoice) : Result<LibraryVersionRef, PublishError>`, each in this order. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it answers `PromotionKitErr (KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr "promoteToLibrary"))`, reading and writing nothing, because the put comes before the snapshot that would refuse. Then the promoted value: `study.promotedMaterialWith run version entry` or `run.promotedBlackBoxWith item choice` (step 407). Its entry id: `version.materialId.toLibraryEntryId` (step 24) or `item.id.toLibraryEntryId` (step 407). Its version: `VersionNumber.first` when `this.imports.proxy.tryHeldEntry` of the id (step 94) answers `None`, a black box promoted for the first time being a new entry, and `held.latest.next` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:VersionNumber.next`) otherwise; a read error is `PromotionImportErr`. Its content: `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry <the version> (run.provenanceIn this.kit.kitFile.id) <the promoted entry>` (steps 25, 355: a crystal writes `CrystalMaterialPayload`) or `LibraryEntryContent.ofPolarizerPreset <the version> <that provenance> <the preset>` (step 25), its error `PromotionEntryErr`. `this.imports.sealEntry` of it and `this.imports.proxy.putEntryVersion { envelope = <the sealed envelope>; latest = MoveLatestVersion }` (step 94), either error `PromotionImportErr`. Then `this.snapshotReferences [ EntryVersionReference { entryId = <the id>; version = <the version> } ]` (steps 137, 139), its error `PromotionKitErr`. The answer is that `LibraryVersionRef`. The version the study opened stays as it was and pinned (step 359), so the study and every sample that names it are unchanged, while the library database answers the promoted version as the entry's latest (001 §C). Nothing is replaced or deleted, so no undo is needed. No other member, retry or option is added. Tests, in `StudyPublishingTests`, each fact over a fresh `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), disposed at its end: a `KitLibraryContext` whose kit is `KitProxy.createInMemory` of an initialised `InMemoryKitFolder` opened read-write through `KitContext.openKit` with a stepping clock, as `StudyMessageTests` opens its kits (step 366), and whose imports are `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase <the database>)` (step 95); a user absorbing crystal material saved through `(MaterialProxy.createInDatabase <the database>).saveMaterial` (step 69) at version 1, opened by the study and recorded through `recordStudy` (steps 359, 361), which pins it; and step 407's runs. `promoting a fitted material mints its next library version under the fit's provenance and snapshots it into the kit`: `promoteMaterial` answers version 2 of the material; `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase`'s `resolveVersion` answers the promoted entry for version 2 and the saved one for version 1; `imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` of version 2 (step 105) holds `FitProvenance` of the kit file's id, `FileStem "QZ-LR"` and the run's stem; and the kit's `paths` hold `library/<the GUID>@v2.material-json` beside `library/<the GUID>@v1.material-json`. `promoting a black box adds a custom-Mueller preset at version 1, and promoting it again mints version 2`: `promoteBlackBox` of QZ (step 407's black box, its choice `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId)`) answers version 1 under QZ's GUID, the kit holding `library/<QZ's GUID>@v1.polarizer-json`; promoting it again from a second run of the study answers version 2, and the kit holds both snapshots. `a read-only kit promotes nothing`: over a context whose kit is opened `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, both members answer `PromotionKitErr` of `KitReadOnlyErr`, `tryHeldEntry` answers what it answered before, and `paths` and every file's bytes are unchanged. `every publish error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the mint lands, `KitLibraryContext.promoteMaterial` and `promoteBlackBox` MUST write the promoted value as its entry's next version (version 1 for a new black-box entry) through the import seam under `FitProvenance`, MUST snapshot and pin that version into the kit, and MUST write nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `promoting a fitted material mints its next library version under the fit's provenance and snapshots it into the kit`, `promoting a black box adds a custom-Mueller preset at version 1, and promoting it again mints version 2` and `a read-only kit promotes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
